From 2874b0fed2f7f7ab8b1e751b645314d0916774a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 23:42:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm, settings: Dolby Vision sent in IPT by default,
 as licensed players send it

videoscreen.hadesdvtransport takes a third value. 0, the default, is now
"As licensed players send (IPT)" (#39898, Estuary #32006): profiles 7 and 8
go out in IPT-PQ-c2 (dvbridge_render_use_ipt()), profile 5 as before. "As
composed" (#39896) moves to value 2 and keeps sending the composer's YCbCr;
"Converted to BT.2020" stays 1. A setting left at its default takes the new
default; one set to converted keeps it. The help says what each sends
(en_gb, es_es, es_ar, es_mx).

kodi.log says, in the 10-s line of native Dolby Vision, how many frames went
out in IPT and how many in the composer's YCbCr (the last level of the
fidelity step-down sends that one where the graphics cannot keep up), next
to the GPU time and the level of those frames; the line of the first frame
of a stream says "in IPT-PQ-c2, as licensed players send it", and the
Dolby Vision page of the player information shows the value of the setting.
The comments no longer say "as certified source devices send it".
