@@ -25641,7 +25641,7 @@ msgstr ""
 #. Hades: help of setting "videoscreen.hadesdvtransport"; translated in Estuary (#32001)
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 msgctxt "#39895"
-msgid "For experts. How native Dolby Vision is sent to the TV. As composed: the picture that the composer of ETSI GS CCM 001 builds, as it is, in the colour representation that the video describes (YCbCr, or IPT for profile 5), with metadata that describes it, as clause 6 of that specification describes; where the menus or subtitles are drawn over the video, those pixels are converted back into that representation. Converted to BT.2020: the picture is rebuilt in RGB and converted to BT.2020 YCbCr, as earlier builds sent it, to compare the two on a display. A video that is scaled to the screen (a 1080p one), or rebuilt by libplacebo's reshaping, goes out converted either way. What the fidelity step-down finds is not kept while Converted to BT.2020 is chosen. Applies from the next video."
+msgid "For experts. How native Dolby Vision is sent to the TV. As licensed players send (IPT), the default: the picture that the composer of ETSI GS CCM 001 builds, converted to IPT-PQ-c2 for profiles 7 and 8, as licensed players are reported to send every profile (profile 5 is IPT already), with metadata that describe it; where a graphics chip cannot keep up, the automatic fidelity step-down sends it as composed at its last level. As composed: that picture as it is, in the colour representation that the video describes (YCbCr, or IPT for profile 5), as clause 6 of that specification allows. Converted to BT.2020: the picture is rebuilt in RGB and converted to BT.2020 YCbCr, as earlier builds sent it, to compare on a display. Where menus or subtitles are drawn over the video, those pixels are converted into the representation that is sent. What the fidelity step-down finds is not kept while Converted to BT.2020 is chosen. Applies from the next video."
 msgstr ""
 
 #. Hades: value of setting "videoscreen.hadesdvtransport": the composer's picture as it is, as clause 6 of ETSI GS CCM 001 describes (the default); also on the Dolby Vision page of the player information; translated in Estuary (#32002)
@@ -25656,7 +25656,13 @@ msgctxt "#39897"
 msgid "Converted to BT.2020"
